TEXT 96 -96 Left 2 ;First-order sigma-delta ADC in two Verilog blocks. Modulator: R1 carries the current of Vin and R2 the one of the feedback fb into node «int», and C1 integrates them;\nMODULATOR (the 1-bit quantizer) compares «int» with vcc/2 on each clock edge: above it, y = 1 and fb goes to 0 and discharges C1; below it, y = 0 and fb goes to 1 and charges it.\nSo «int» stays near 2.5 V, the average of fb follows 5 V − Vin and the fraction of ones in the stream y is Vin / 5 V. DOWNSAMPLER turns that 1 MHz stream into 7-bit words.
TEXT 1008 416 Left 2 ;DOWNSAMPLER: every 64 clock cycles it puts on the bus d[6:0]\nhow many ones came in on y (0 … 64): 15.6 kS/s.
TEXT 160 624 Left 2 ;7-bit R-2R DAC: each bit of the bus d[6:0] goes in through a 20k; out = 5 V · code / 128 ≈ Vin/2
TEXT 160 1008 Left 2 !.tran 8m
